cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it."
title: "SattvaRoute: Evidence-driven physical-design diagnosis and controlled recovery for VLSI implementation workflows"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "SattvaRoute contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-18
repository-code: "https://github.com/RAMA-L7/SattvaRoute"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - physical design
  - EDA
  - OpenROAD
  - AI agents
  - failure diagnosis
  - reproducibility
abstract: >
  SattvaRoute is a research-grade framework for evidence-driven physical-design
  diagnosis and controlled recovery. It orchestrates OpenROAD-flow stages with
  preserved run evidence, deterministically diagnoses bounded failures, requires
  explicit human approval for exact-patch changes, executes isolated
  stage-limited recovery attempts, and independently verifies outcomes. Model
  assistance is optional and advisory; no signoff or general AI competence is
  claimed.
